src/
└── com.indianbazar
    ├── model            # All POJO classes (Product, User, etc.)
    ├── service          # Interfaces like ProductService, UserService
    ├── service.impl     # Implementations of the service interfaces
    ├── controller       # Menu-driven logic or console simulation (optional for now)
    └── main             # Main entry point to run and test the app

    

| Class Name | Purpose                                                    |
| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| `Product`  | Defines all product-related fields (id, name, price, etc.) |
| `User`     | Defines user fields like id, name, email, password, role   |


| Interface Name   | Purpose                                             |
| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `ProductService` | Declares methods for product operations             |
| `UserService`    | Declares methods for user registration, login, etc. |


| Class Name           | Purpose                                                              |
| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `ProductServiceImpl` | Implements logic to store, update, delete products using collections |
| `UserServiceImpl`    | Implements user-related logic (register/login) using a Map or List   |


| Class Name       | Purpose                                                                              |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `IndianBazarApp` | Entry point of the application with `main()` method to simulate product/user actions |




1. Backend Setup
Model Class: Product.java (with fields like id, name, description, price, imageUrl, category)

Repository: ProductRepository.java

Service & Impl: To fetch products by category

Controller: /api/products?category=Electronics

2. Database Sample Data
Add 10 sample records per category in product_inventory_db

We’ll use either data.sql or a Spring Boot initializer method to pre-populate.

3. Frontend
On clicking a category (e.g., "Electronics"), make a fetch call to /api/products?category=Electronics and render the data dynamically, including images.


<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Login - IndianBazar</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/frontend/styles.css">
</head>
<body>

  <!-- Navbar -->
  <div class="navbar">
    <div class="left">
      <a href="/frontend/index.html">IndianBazar</a>
    </div>
    <div class="right">
      <a href="/frontend/login.html">Login</a>
      <a href="/frontend/signup.html">SignUp</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Login Form -->
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Login</h2>
    <form id="loginForm" novalidate>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="email">Email</label>
        <input type="email" id="email" required>
        <div id="emailError" class="error-message"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="password">Password</label>
        <input type="password" id="password" required>
        <div id="passwordError" class="error-message"></div>
      </div>

      <button type="submit">Login</button>
    </form>
  </div>

  <script>
    document.getElementById("loginForm").addEventListener("submit", function (e) {
      e.preventDefault();

      const email = document.getElementById("email");
      const password = document.getElementById("password");

      const emailError = document.getElementById("emailError");
      const passwordError = document.getElementById("passwordError");

      emailError.textContent = "";
      passwordError.textContent = "";

      let valid = true;

      const emailPattern = /^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$/;
      if (!emailPattern.test(email.value.trim())) {
        emailError.textContent = "Please enter a valid email address.";
        valid = false;
      }

      if (password.value.trim().length < 6) {
        passwordError.textContent = "Password must be at least 6 characters.";
        valid = false;
      }

      if (valid) {
        alert("✅ Login successful (frontend validation passed)");
        // Simulate redirect or further logic
        // window.location.href = "/frontend/index.html";
      }
    });
  </script>

</body>
</html>
